4:["$","strong",null,{"children":"Equated Monthly Installment"}]
5:["$","ol",null,{"className":"mt-4 list-decimal space-y-2 pl-6 text-slate-700","children":["\n",["$","li",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Interest"}]," on the outstanding balance (large at the start), and"]}],"\n",["$","li",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Principal repayment"}]," (small at the start, growing every month)."]}],"\n"]}]
6:["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-4 leading-relaxed text-slate-700","children":"Because the interest portion shrinks as you pay down the balance, the same\nmonthly amount slowly shifts from \"mostly interest\" to \"mostly principal\" —\nthis is called amortization."}]
7:["$","h2",null,{"className":"mt-10 text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-slate-900","children":"The formula"}]
8:["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-4 leading-relaxed text-slate-700","children":"The standard amortization formula for a fixed-rate loan is:"}]
9:["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-4 leading-relaxed text-slate-700","children":["$","code",null,{"className":"rounded bg-slate-100 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-slate-800","children":"EMI = P × r × (1 + r)ⁿ ÷ ((1 + r)ⁿ − 1)"}]}]
a:["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-4 leading-relaxed text-slate-700","children":"Where:"}]
b:["$","ul",null,{"className":"mt-4 list-disc space-y-2 pl-6 text-slate-700","children":["\n",["$","li",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"P"}]," is the principal (the amount you actually borrow, not the car price),"]}],"\n",["$","li",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"r"}]," is the ",["$","strong",null,{"children":"monthly"}]," interest rate (annual rate ÷ 12 ÷ 100), and"]}],"\n",["$","li",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"n"}]," is the number of monthly installments (years × 12)."]}],"\n"]}]
c:["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-4 leading-relaxed text-slate-700","children":["The most common mistake is plugging in the annual rate directly. The formula\nneeds the monthly rate — for an 11% loan that is 0.11 ÷ 12 = ",["$","strong",null,{"children":"0.009167"}],"."]}]
d:["$","h2",null,{"className":"mt-10 text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-slate-900","children":"A worked example with Nepali numbers"}]
e:["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-4 leading-relaxed text-slate-700","children":"Suppose you are buying a car invoiced at Rs. 42,00,000. The bank agrees to\nfinance 80%, so your down payment is Rs. 8,40,000 and the loan amount is:"}]
f:["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-4 leading-relaxed text-slate-700","children":["$","code",null,{"className":"rounded bg-slate-100 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-slate-800","children":"P = Rs. 33,60,000"}]}]
10:["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-4 leading-relaxed text-slate-700","children":"Assume an 11% annual rate (typical for auto loans from commercial banks in\nNepal in recent years) and a 5-year tenure:"}]
11:["$","ul",null,{"className":"mt-4 list-disc space-y-2 pl-6 text-slate-700","children":["\n",["$","li",null,{"children":"r = 11 ÷ 12 ÷ 100 = 0.009167"}],"\n",["$","li",null,{"children":"n = 5 × 12 = 60 months"}],"\n",["$","li",null,{"children":"(1 + r)ⁿ ≈ 1.7289"}],"\n"]}]
12:["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-4 leading-relaxed text-slate-700","children":["$","code",null,{"className":"rounded bg-slate-100 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-slate-800","children":"EMI = 33,60,000 × 0.009167 × 1.7289 ÷ (1.7289 − 1) ≈ Rs. 73,050"}]}]
13:["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-4 leading-relaxed text-slate-700","children":["So the bank takes roughly ",["$","strong",null,{"children":"Rs. 73,050 every month for 60 months"}],". The total\nyou repay is 73,050 × 60 = ",["$","strong",null,{"children":"Rs. 43,83,000"}],", which means the interest cost of\nthe loan is about ",["$","strong",null,{"children":"Rs. 10,23,000"}]," — nearly a third of the car's price."]}]
14:["$","div",null,{"className":"my-8 rounded-xl border border-amber-200 bg-amber-50 p-5","children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"flex items-center gap-2 text-sm font-bold text-amber-800","children":[["$","$L3",null,{"iconNode":[["path",{"d":"M15 14c.2-1 .7-1.7 1.5-2.5 1-.9 1.5-2.2 1.5-3.5A6 6 0 0 0 6 8c0 1 .2 2.2 1.5 3.5.7.7 1.3 1.5 1.5 2.5","key":"1gvzjb"}],["path",{"d":"M9 18h6","key":"x1upvd"}],["path",{"d":"M10 22h4","key":"ceow96"}]],"className":"lucide-lightbulb h-4 w-4"}],"Worth knowing"]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-amber-900/90","children":["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-4 leading-relaxed text-slate-700","children":"In lakh-style grouping (the en-IN locale used across this site for Nepal and\nIndia), the monthly figure reads Rs. 73,050 and the interest reads Rs.\n10,23,000 — always double-check which grouping a figure uses before comparing\noffers."}]}]]}]
15:["$","h2",null,{"className":"mt-10 text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-slate-900","children":"The five inputs that move your EMI"}]
16:["$","ul",null,{"className":"mt-4 list-disc space-y-2 pl-6 text-slate-700","children":["\n",["$","li",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Loan amount, not car price."}]," A bigger down payment shrinks P and cuts\ninterest for the entire tenure, not just the first year."]}],"\n",["$","li",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Interest rate."}]," On this example, moving from 11% to 12.5% pushes the EMI\nto roughly Rs. 75,600 — over Rs. 1.5 lakh more interest across the life of\nthe loan. Always compare the ",["$","em",null,{"children":"effective"}]," rate including processing fees."]}],"\n",["$","li",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Tenure."}]," Stretching 5 years to 7 years lowers the EMI but raises total\ninterest sharply, because interest compounds over more months."]}],"\n",["$","li",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Fixed vs. floating rate."}]," Many Nepali auto loans are floating, repriced\nagainst the bank's base rate. Ask how often the rate reviews and what your\nEMI would be at base rate + 3%."]}],"\n",["$","li",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Fees."}]," Processing fees (often ~1%), insurance requirements and prepayment\npenalties change the ",["$","em",null,{"children":"effective"}]," cost even when they do not change the EMI."]}],"\n"]}]
17:["$","h2",null,{"className":"mt-10 text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-slate-900","children":"How to use the calculator"}]
18:["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-4 leading-relaxed text-slate-700","children":["Open the ",["$","a",null,{"className":"font-medium text-indigo-600 underline decoration-indigo-300 underline-offset-4 transition-colors hover:text-indigo-800","href":"/tools/finance/loan-calculator","children":"Loan Calculator"}],", enter the amount\nyou plan to borrow (car price minus your down payment), your bank's annual\nrate, and the tenure in years. It returns the monthly payment, total interest\nand total repayment instantly — so you can compare a 5-year and a 7-year\noffer, or two banks' rates, in seconds."]}]
